From 2bf41934a0c1a5f2b986d7df8cb76d0a73cf4724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:03:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] feat(algorithm): StockhamFFT for complex power-of-two
 sizes at native simd width
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`gr::algorithm::FFT` routes complex power-of-two transforms of at least 64 points to `StockhamFFT` where the `std::simd` backend is native, through a `constexpr` route table per type and vector width; everything else stays on `SimdFFT`.

```cpp
gr::algorithm::StockhamFFT<float> fft;
fft.resize(1024UZ);                  // default plan {8, 16, 8}
fft.resize(1024UZ, std::array{8UZ, 8UZ, 16UZ}); // explicit radix plan, checked by isValidPlan
fft.forward(in, out);                // unnormalised, in == out allowed
```

Stockham autosort [Stockham 1966; Van Loan 1992], interleaved complex data, radix-8 first pass with an in-register transpose, radix 2/4/8/16 later passes vectorised over the stride.
C++23: vir/libstdc++ `native_simd`, two-input shuffles via `__builtin_shufflevector` on the same-width vector type.
C++26 preview (`__cpp_lib_simd`): `std::simd::vec`, `permute` and `cat`, no compiler extensions.

### Changes
- `StockhamFFT.hpp`: kernel, plans (`defaultPlan`, `isValidPlan`), C++23 and C++26 backends
- `fft.hpp`: `FFTRoute` tables and `fftRoute<T>(N)`; at 128-bit vectors N > 2^14 stays on `SimdFFT` (measured, HX 370)
- `qa_StockhamFFT.cpp`: long-double DFT ground truth 2^6–2^16 (2^20 double), every valid plan, in-place, impulse and tone, routing
- `bm_FFT_backends.cpp`: CPU row labelled `FFT (CPU)`
